This example demonstrates a 2D finite-strain isochoric Standard Linear Solid (SLS)
viscoelastic body under simple-shear stress relaxation using IBFEMethod on a
QUAD9 mesh (`G_INF = 1.0`, `G_SLS = 2.0`, `TAU_R = 0.05`, `GAMMA_0 = 0.12`).

Model helper (`IBFEViscoelasticity.h`):
Implements an objective generalized Maxwell internal-variable formulation on the
isochoric second Piola-Kirchhoff target `S_{m,iso}(C)` pushed forward from the
dev_C-projected overstress, using a second-order exponential linear-ramp
integrator (`phi_1`, `psi_1`, with 5-term Taylor series for small `|x|`).
`GeneralizedMaxwellHistoryStore` stores committed per-quadrature-point history,
keeps trial PK1 evaluations read-only during RK2 substeps, advances history
once per accepted step, and gathers sorted slot keys collectively across MPI
ranks during SAMRAI restart serialization (`putToDatabase` / `getFromDatabase`).

Quadrature note:
Because `IBFEMethod::registerPK1StressFunction` passes reference coordinate `s`
without a quadrature-point index, `example.cpp` passes fixed non-adaptive
quadrature (`QP_TYPE = QGAUSS`, `QP_ORDER = FIFTH`) directly to
`IBFEMethod::PK1StressFcnData` so `findNearestSlotIndex` matches every Gauss
point directly (falling back to the equilibrium branch for non-Gauss
evaluations).
